  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting wild populations of Encephalartos cycad species and strengthening enforcement capacity by harnessing forensic capabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to counter wildlife trafficking in South.Africa by supporting the criminal justice system. This project is intended to conserve Encephalartos cycad species by addressing the impact of illegal harvesting and trafficking. Specific activities include: (1.1) Identification of a government approved laboratory designated to receive and process cycad DNA samples; (1.2) Develop and agree on National Cycad DNA chain of evidence standard operating procedures; (2.1) Procure DNA voucher specimen kits;.(2.2) Procure DNA crime scene kits; (3.1) Provide DNA evidence collection training; (3.2) Provide advanced cycad enforcement training; (3.3) Provide awareness raising for state prosecutors and magistrates; (4.1) Collect cycad DNA samples from wild cycad populations; (4.2) Strengthen the cycad DNA reference library; and, (4.3) Research individual cycad DNA fingerprinting. (4.2) Strengthen the cycad DNA reference library; and, (4.3) Research individual cycad DNA.fingerprinting.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
